= Artifact [AT-nn] =

//The Prototype, Simulation, or other tangible Implementation evaluated this cycle. It instantiates a specific set of Use Cases and, through them, the Functions, Premises, and Claims those Use Cases carry, so they can be evaluated in a controlled Evaluation.//

**How to use this page:** Duplicate it once per Artifact you build (usually just one per project, revised across Builds rather than replaced). Fill in every field below; write “not applicable” rather than leaving a field blank. Rename the page title to a short, human-readable name for this Artifact and record its ID (AT-01, AT-02…) in the table.

|**ID**|Stable identifier, unique within this entity type (e.g. AT-01, AT-02…).
\\[ fill in ]
|**Name**|A short, human-readable label for this instance.
\\[ fill in ]
|**Status**|Not Started / In Progress / Under Review / In Evaluation / Finalized.
\\[ fill in ]
|**Scope**|Which Functions it implements, and which are deliberately out of scope.
\\[ fill in ]
|**Simulation notice**|If a Simulation substitutes for part of the interaction, what it does and does not simulate. Write “not applicable” where no Simulation is used.
\\[ fill in ]
|**Premises verifiable**|Which Premises this build makes verifiable, and which are assumed rather than testable with it.
\\[ fill in ]
|**Builds**|One row per build evaluated this cycle: a short label, and what changed from the previous build. Evaluation Reports cite a build by this label, so the Verification and Validation Summary can tell which Evidence speaks to the current version.(((
|=Build|=What changed
|[ e.g. Build A ]|[ fill in ]
|[ e.g. Build B ]|[ fill in ]
)))

**Graph edges:** //instantiates → Use Case; used-by ← Evaluation Report.//